    id: "x4-37-cpzczg",
    chapter: 37,
    block: 4,
    stem: "A 22-year-old patient is involved. A home-care patient with a tracheostomy has noisy, gurgling respirations and falling oxygen saturation. You suction the tube. Which technique is correct?",
    choices: [
      "Suction continuously for up to 30 seconds while advancing deep past the tube",
      "Apply suction only while withdrawing, limiting each attempt to 10 seconds",
      "Instill 20 milliliters of saline first, then suction on insertion and withdrawal",
      "Remove the entire tracheostomy tube before suctioning the open stoma",
    ],
